{
  "set": "composite_trust_query_lite",
  "schema_version": "composite_trust_query_lite/v1",
  "description": "Open, content-addressed trust-verdict references over the AlgoVoi substrate (RFC 8785 JCS + SHA-256). trust_query_ref = \"sha256:\" + SHA-256(JCS({subject_refs, trust_outcome})). subject_refs is the ordered list of references the verdict was reached over, each imported by hash; tq-001/002/003 assess the full live decision chain [passport_ref, mandate_ref, policy_bound_ref, guardrail_ref(ALLOW)] from spend_decision_chain_v1, so this caps the open lifecycle. Both order and membership of subject_refs are byte-load-bearing, as is trust_outcome (a closed enum {TRUSTED, PROVISIONAL, INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE, UNTRUSTED}). An outcome outside the enum, an empty subject_refs list, or an empty member is rejected, not hashed. LITE tier binds ONLY; the scoring/verification that produce the verdict stay commercial (the commercial Composite Trust Query walks the audit chain and issues a Falcon-1024 PQC signed verdict).",
  "canonicalizer": "rfc8785-jcs",
  "fields": [
    "subject_refs",
    "trust_outcome"
  ],
  "trust_outcomes": [
    "TRUSTED",
    "PROVISIONAL",
    "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE",
    "UNTRUSTED"
  ],
  "note_chain": "subject_refs [b3594e33.., a4f8cb5e.., aaee2091.., 2a444c62..] are passport_ref + mandate_ref + policy_bound_ref + guardrail_ref(ALLOW) from spend_decision_chain_v1; trust_query_ref binds a categorical verdict to that exact assessed set, capping the lifecycle. tq-keystone extends the cap to the full keystone flow: subject_refs [passport_ref, mandate_ref, policy_bound_ref, decision_ref(ALLOW), execution_ref] spans identity -> authority -> policy -> decision -> execution, so one trust verdict covers the whole chain through the post-decision execution evidence.",
